    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1991-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Dividing both numerator and denominator by the nonzero number \\(b\\) gives \\[ \\frac{a+b}{a-b}=\\frac{\\frac{a}{b}+1}{\\frac{a}{b}-1}=\\frac{x+1}{x-1}. \\]\n\nThus the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Divide the numerator and denominator by \\(b\\)",
        "Replace each occurrence of \\(\\frac{a}{b}\\) by \\(x\\)"
      ],
